§ `30. obstruction`

`30(1)(a)` MEANS `Obstruction Facts` WITH
    `the accused obstructed an officer of the Bureau, police officer, officer of customs or other public officer in the exercise of a power under this Act` IS TRUE
    `the accused failed to comply with a lawful requirement of such an officer in the execution of his or her duty under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed to furnish information in his or her possession required by such an officer` IS FALSE
    `the accused furnished to such an officer information which he or she knew or had reason to believe to be false` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `an offence under section 30(1)(a) is made out` `30(1)(a)`

#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 30(1)(b) is made out` `30(1)(a)`

#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 30(1)(c) is made out` `30(1)(a)`

#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 30(1)(d) is made out` `30(1)(a)`

`30(1)(b)` MEANS `Obstruction Facts` WITH
